// treated as FINAL PROTOTYPE TRUTH, subject to the mandatory restrictions the
// user confirmed: exclude every unresolved source conflict, exclude
// confidential/live operational data, never silently resolve a contradiction,
// never present a worked example as universal policy, and never introduce PPC
// knowledge from outside these sources. See
// docs/centralized-ppc-team-source-map.md for the full 30-file inventory and
// docs/centralized-ppc-team-exclusions.md for the complete exclusions register.
//
// MANDATORY CONFLICT EXCLUSIONS APPLIED THROUGHOUT (never taught, never
// quizzed, never used in the practical task):
//  1. the disputed Amazon SP minimum star-rating figure (two different values
//     found across two Amazon BGCT sources);
//  2. the disputed Amazon budget-review cadence (two different cadences found
//     across two Amazon BGCT sources);
//  3. the Amazon "ASINs per ad group" internal contradiction (one Amazon
//     source states two different rules against itself);
//  4. the disputed Amazon UK vs. DE/FR/IT high-ACOS pause threshold (two
//     different values for what should be the same rule);
//  5. the un-localised currency found in several Amazon DE/FR/IT workflow
//     documents (thresholds priced in the wrong currency for their market);
//  6. the disputed month-boundary split date used to choose between a 30-day
//     and a month-to-date ACOS figure (two different cut-off days found
//     across sibling Amazon UK workflows);
//  7. the disputed "fast-moving product" definition (two different sets of
//     qualifying conditions found across sibling Amazon UK workflows);
//  8. the disputed eBay advertising-rate guidance (two individually authored
//     eBay sources give directly contradictory starting/ceiling rate advice);
//  9. the disputed Amazon budget-tier structure (the number and shape of
//     performance tiers used for budget adjustment differs between sibling
//     Amazon UK workflows for what should be the same rule family).
// Where a lesson below touches one of these nine topics, it teaches only the
// underlying, non-conflicting concept (for example, "campaigns are grouped by
// ACOS performance and each group receives a different budget response") and
// never states the disputed number, range, or structure as settled fact.
//
// CONFIDENTIALITY: no real advertising account, client, or seller name; no
// account/campaign/ad-group/portfolio ID; no live ASIN, SKU, or eBay Item ID;
// no real budget, spend, sales, or account-level ACOS/TACOS/ROAS/CPA/CPC
// figure; and no named individual staff member appears anywhere below. Every
// example is fictional and neutral. Where a source names an individual in a
// governance role (for example, an Amazon Document Control owner, a Google
// Ads Team Lead, an eBay "Leader"), this programme uses the generic role
// title only.

const PROGRAMME_ID = 'centralized-ppc-team';

const module = (id, orderIndex, title, summary, estimatedMinutes, source, prerequisiteModuleIds) => ({
  id,
  programmeId: PROGRAMME_ID,
  orderIndex,
  title,
  summary,
  estimatedMinutes,
  prerequisiteModuleIds: prerequisiteModuleIds || [],
  // User-confirmed: Centralized PPC Team requires NO learner or reviewer sign-off.
  requiresSignoff: false,
  status: 'FINAL_TRUTH',
  source,
});

const lesson = (id, moduleId, orderIndex, title, content, estimatedMinutes, source) => ({
  id,
  moduleId,
  orderIndex,
  title,
  content,
  estimatedMinutes,
  required: true,
  status: 'FINAL_TRUTH',
  source,
});

